        "original_id": "8cc687f6-5773-5853-8293-b6935c7cd2b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Boots Randolph, Fats Domino, Sandy Nelson, Wayne Fontana, Herbie Hancock, George Porter Jr., Zigaboo Modeliste, Sheryl Crow, Paul McCartney, Renard Poché\n- Groups: The Mindbenders, Defenders, Asleep at the Wheel, Orion\n- Songs: \"I'm Gonna Be a Wheel Someday\", \"Yakety Sax\"\n- Topics: cover versions, Nashville sound\n\nFacts:\n- \"I'm Gonna Be a Wheel Someday\" was later covered by Fats Domino, Sandy Nelson, Wayne Fontana and the Mindbenders, Boots Randolph, Defenders, Asleep at the Wheel, Orion, and Herbie Hancock with George Porter Jr., Zigaboo Modeliste, Sheryl Crow, Paul McCartney, and Renard Poché.\n- Homer Louis \"Boots\" Randolph III was born on June 3, 1927, and died on July 3, 2007.\n- Boots Randolph was an American musician best known for his 1963 saxophone hit \"Yakety Sax\".\n- \"Yakety Sax\" became Benny Hill's signature tune.\n- Boots Randolph was a major part of the Nashville sound for most of his professional career.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
